Our progress -
We created a GameControlPanel class using Java Swing. Our control panel includes buttons for moving to the next player 
and making an accusation, along with fields displaying the current player's turn, dice roll, guesses, and guess results. 
We also implemented setter methods to update the information displayed in each field. We used GridLayout and FlowLayout to
organize the components and created a main method to test the panel independently in a JFrame. Our layout is similar to the 
instructor's example.
